			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1772865070277,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "ACID works well for single database systems, but when systems become large and distributed, maintaining\nstrict ACID guarantees becomes very difficult.\n\nBASE is a set of properties used in distributed systems that prioritize availability and scalability over\nstrict consistency.\n\nSo many large systems adopt BASE, where:\nsystem stays available\nconsistency becomes eventual",
			"rawText": "ACID works well for single database systems, but when systems become large and distributed, maintaining strict ACID guarantees becomes very difficult.\n\nBASE is a set of properties used in distributed systems that prioritize availability and scalability over strict consistency.\n\nSo many large systems adopt BASE, where:\nsystem stays available\nconsistency becomes eventual",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"fontFamily": 8,
			"textAlign": "center",
			"verticalAlign": "middle",
			"containerId": "dr5Gg51O",
			"originalText": "ACID works well for single database systems, but when systems become large and distributed, maintaining strict ACID guarantees becomes very difficult.\n\nBASE is a set of properties used in distributed systems that prioritize availability and scalability over strict consistency.\n\nSo many large systems adopt BASE, where:\nsystem stays available\nconsistency becomes eventual",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"link": null
		},
